Changes of the Raku package "Math::NIntegrate".

0.0.3 2026-10-02
    - Process user specified "singular points" given in the range specs
      - For example:
      - nintegrate({1/(1-$^x).abs.sqrt}, <x 0 1 2>)
      - nintegrate({1/($^x + $^y).abs.sqrt}, <x -1 0 1>, <y -1 0 1>)
    - Fixes for both concise- and multi-component Cartesian rule specifications
    - Facilitation of stepping away from singular points during integrand evaluation
    - Special representation methods -- gist, Hash, Str -- for strategies and rules

0.0.2 2026-10-01
    - Implemented LocalAdaptive integration strategy
      - Related region division implementation and grammar/interpreter extensions.

0.0.1 2026-09-28
    - First version with:
        - GlobalAdaptive integration strategy
            - Can be given an integration monitor routine as an argument.
        - The integration rules:
            - Cartesian, ClenshawCurtis, GaussKronrod, MonteCarlo, MultiDimensional, NewtonCotes, Trapezoidal
        - Singularity handler by Iri, Moriguti, & Takesawa ("IMT rule").
        - Comprehensive integrator spec parsing and interpretation
        - Kahaner integrator tests
        - CLI script
